<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qajar dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Qajars, Qajar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Qajar dynasty was a Turkmen dynasty that ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> from the late eighteenth century until 1925. Its founder Agha Mohammad Khan defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zand-dynasty">Zand Empire</a> and in 1796 took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mashhad">Mashhad</a>, ending the last remnant of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire</a>. The Qajars reunified Iran but faced growing pressure from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty.jpg" alt="Qajar dynasty" width="320" height="385" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alexander Fadeyev (Faddeyev) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Persia_(endonym;_Iran)_in_the_1860s.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
